1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,925
What if every chip on Earth stopped working, all at once?

2
00:00:03,417 --> 00:00:04,865
Phones die instantly.

3
00:00:04,865 --> 00:00:08,798
So do laptops, the internet, card payments, and most TVs.

4
00:00:09,283 --> 00:00:12,734
Modern cars are full of chips, so most won't start.

5
00:00:12,734 --> 00:00:13,275
In 2021,

6
00:00:13,275 --> 00:00:19,431
just a shortage of chips cost carmakers about two hundred and ten billion dollars in sales.

7
00:00:19,917 --> 00:00:24,240
Power grids, water pumps and traffic lights lean on electronic controls too.

8
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:25,947
So the lights start going out.

9
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:27,673
What still works?

10
00:00:27,673 --> 00:00:28,753
Wind-up clocks.

11
00:00:28,753 --> 00:00:29,401
Bicycles.

12
00:00:29,401 --> 00:00:31,488
Old cars with no electronics.

13
00:00:31,488 --> 00:00:34,582
And antique radios built with vacuum tubes.

14
00:00:35,083 --> 00:00:41,567
Tubes are so tough that a Soviet fighter jet was still flying with tube electronics in the 1970s.

15
00:00:42,083 --> 00:00:44,796
So what if the transistor was never invented?

16
00:00:44,796 --> 00:00:46,363
Full story on the channel.
